§§ DESIGN-PILLARS
  a llama.cpp via subprocess ← reproducible • offline • CI-friendly
  b multi-model agreement ← ≥ 3 models • inter-model variance
  c token-level NLL ← per-token surprise ¬ file-aggregate-only
  d statistical rigor ← bootstrap CI • hold-out cross-validation
  e per-mode stratification ← pure-CSL • bridge • prose (matches m₁)
  f comparison-harness ← vs APL/J/k • Lojban • prose-baseline
  g paraphrase-quality scoring ← Apocky-reviewed + algorithmic
  h reproducibility ← checkpoint-SHA-pinning + temp=0 + seed-fixed
  i visualization ← per-token surprise-heatmap HTML-report
  j audit-chain ← Ed25519 reuse from smt_audit pattern

§§ DEFINITION (formalized)
  m₂ ≡ mean-NLL(CSL-form) / mean-NLL(EN-paraphrase)
  where :
    NLL(seq, model) = -Σᵢ log P(tokenᵢ | token<ᵢ ; model)
    mean-NLL = NLL / |tokens|
  interpretation :
    m₂ < 1.0  : CSL more-predictable than EN ← unlikely (rare-glyphs)
    m₂ ≈ 1.0  : equal-density
    m₂ ≤ 1.2  : target ← CSL ≤ 1.2× EN-perplexity
    m₂ > 1.5  : CSL too-surprising ← model unfamiliar with-notation
    m₂ > 2.0  : likely-failure of-density-claim
  caveat :
    pre-trained models have-EN-bias ← m₂ ≥ 1.0 expected
    m₂ measures relative-density not absolute-quality
    multi-model evaluation reduces single-model bias

§§ FILES-NEW
  scripts/compute_m2.py                ~600-LOC  core m₂ harness
    multi-model dispatch + token-level NLL collection
    per-file + per-mode reporting
    bootstrap CI computation
    deterministic seed + temp=0 enforcement
  scripts/m2_models.py                 ~300-LOC  model registry
    model checkpoint URLs + SHA-256 pins
    download-or-verify mechanism
    GGUF-format llama.cpp models
    initial set : 3 models @ {1B, 3B, 7B} param-counts
  scripts/m2_visualize.py              ~500-LOC  HTML reporter
    per-token NLL → color-coded heatmap
    side-by-side CSL vs EN-paraphrase
    summary tables with bootstrap-CI
    SVG charts for per-mode breakdown
  scripts/m2_compare.py                ~400-LOC  comparison harness
    same-content via multiple-notations
    metrics : tokens-per-sentence • NLL-per-token • compression-ratio
    notation-set : CSL • APL-fragment • Lojban • prose
    per-content-type stratification
  scripts/m2_quality.py                ~300-LOC  paraphrase-quality
    semantic-similarity via embedding-cosine
    info-preservation check (entity overlap)
    flag low-quality paraphrases for-Apocky-review
  scripts/m2_audit.py                  ~250-LOC  audit-chain integration
    Ed25519-signed m₂-run records
    chain-format : (model-hash, file-hash, m₂, timestamp, signature)
    replay-verify command
    reuse smt_audit infrastructure pattern
  scripts/m2_install_models.sh         ~150-LOC  model bootstrap
    download GGUF checkpoints
    SHA-256 verify
    cache-dir : ~/.cslv3-m2-models/
    skip if-cached
  eval/paraphrases/C1.en               manual EN paraphrase of C1_sort
  eval/paraphrases/C2.en               ... C2_nested_scopes
  eval/paraphrases/C3.en               ... C3_dependent_types
  eval/paraphrases/C4.en               ... C4_reason_block
  eval/paraphrases/C5.en               ... C5_bridge_mode
  eval/paraphrases/C6.en               ... C6_slot_grammar
  eval/paraphrases/C7.en               ... C7_morpheme_stack
  eval/paraphrases/README.md            paraphrase-conventions doc
  eval/m2_baseline.json                 recorded m₂-table per-(file, model)
  eval/m2_results/                      per-run reports (HTML + JSON)
  benchmarks/m2_throughput.md           perf-bench results
  benchmarks/m2_comparison.md           CSL vs APL/Lojban/prose results
  diag/M2_INTERPRETATION.md             how-to-read m₂ + caveats
  specs/15_M2_METRIC.csl                formal metric specification
  tests/test_m2_harness.py             ~300-LOC  smoke + integration
  tests/test_m2_audit.py                ~150-LOC  chain-verify
  tests/m2_fixtures/                    minimal-test fixtures (mock-model)
  CHANGELOG.md                          +Session-11 entry (T25 m₂)

§§ MODEL-SET (initial)
  small  : Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M       ~ 0.9 GB
  medium : Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M       ~ 1.9 GB
  large  : Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3-Q4_K_M    ~ 4.1 GB
  rationale :
    ✓ 3-models = inter-model variance signal
    ✓ different families = reduce single-arch bias
    ✓ Q4_K_M = good quality-vs-size tradeoff
    ✓ all-Apache-2 or-equivalent permissive licenses
    ✓ all available via Hugging Face GGUF mirrors
  selection-criteria :
    multilingual-capable (CSL has Greek + math glyphs)
    instruction-tuned (better at-paraphrase-detection)
    GGUF-available (llama.cpp compatible)
    ≤ 8GB total disk-budget
  N! GPU-only models ← CI-runners CPU-only

§§ ALGORITHM (compute_m2.py core)
  for each (file, model) :
    1 load CSL-content + EN-paraphrase
    2 tokenize via model-native tokenizer
    3 compute logits via llama.cpp eval-callback
    4 NLL_csl = -Σ log P(tokenᵢ|prefix)  on-CSL
    5 NLL_en  = -Σ log P(tokenᵢ|prefix)  on-EN
    6 m₂ = (NLL_csl / |csl-tokens|) / (NLL_en / |en-tokens|)
    7 record per-token NLL for-visualization
    8 record run @ audit-chain
  bootstrap-CI :
    n_resamples = 1000
    per-resample : sample-with-replacement tokens
    compute m₂ on each resample
    report 95% CI from-percentiles

§§ STRATIFICATION-TARGETS
  per-mode m₂ targets ← analogous to m₁ stratification
    | mode      | m₂-target | rationale
    |-----------|-----------|----------
    | pure-CSL  | ≤ 1.5     | dense-glyphs unfamiliar to-LLMs
    | bridge    | ≤ 1.2     | mixed EN+CSL ← LLM-friendly
    | prose     | ≤ 1.05    | mostly-EN ← near-baseline expected
  ∀ targets adjustable post-first-run ← empirical-calibration

§§ COMPARISON-HARNESS (m2_compare.py)
  reference-content : 5 short-passages (algorithm-description category)
    e.g. "binary search • bubble sort • map-reduce • Fibonacci • quicksort"
  notations :
    CSL    : CSLv3 native
    APL    : APL/J/k fragment (handcrafted)
    Lojban : selbri+sumti (constructed-language reference)
    prose  : English-only baseline
  metrics-per-notation :
    token-count
    char-count
    NLL-per-token avg
    NLL-per-content-bit (semantic-density proxy)
  output : benchmarks/m2_comparison.md table
  caveat : APL + Lojban will-have-very-high NLL ← LLM-unfamiliarity
    expected ← demonstrates measurement-uncertainty for-rare-notations

§§ PARAPHRASE-QUALITY (m2_quality.py)
  paraphrase = "what an information-equivalent EN-rendering would-say"
  ¬ word-by-word translation
  ¬ glyph-expansion only
  must-preserve : facts • relationships • inferences-permitted
  scoring :
    embedding-cosine via sentence-transformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
    entity-recall : named-entities both-directions
    flag-low-quality : cosine < 0.7 OR entity-recall < 0.8
  Apocky-review-required for-flagged
  CHANGELOG-entry per-paraphrase-update

§§ AUDIT-CHAIN (m2_audit.py)
  reuse Ed25519 infrastructure from smt_audit.odin pattern
  chain-entry-format :
    {
      prev_hash    : <BLAKE3-of-prev>
      run_id       : <UUID-v4>
      timestamp    : <ISO-8601>
      file_hash    : <SHA-256-of-CSL-file>
      paraphrase_hash : <SHA-256-of-EN-paraphrase>
      model_hash   : <SHA-256-of-GGUF>
      model_name   : <human-readable>
      m2_value     : <float>
      m2_ci_low    : <float>
      m2_ci_high   : <float>
      seed         : <int>
      signature    : <Ed25519>
    }
  storage : .m2-chain/runs.jsonl
  verify-cmd : python scripts/m2_audit.py --verify
  R16-anchor : anyone-can replay + verify

§§ CACHE-DESIGN
  key : BLAKE3(file-content + paraphrase-content + model-hash + algo-version)
  value : (m₂, CI, per-token-NLL, timestamp)
  storage : .m2-cache/<hash>.json
  invalidation : on-model-version-change OR on-paraphrase-change
  CI-restore : cache-restored from-previous-build ← fast incremental

§§ CLI-SURFACE (additive only ← v1.0 stability)
  python scripts/compute_m2.py <file>                     → m₂ all-models
  python scripts/compute_m2.py <file> --model=small        → single model
  python scripts/compute_m2.py <file> --bootstrap=1000     → CI count
  python scripts/compute_m2.py <file> --json               → machine-readable
  python scripts/compute_m2.py --all-eval                  → full corpus
  python scripts/compute_m2.py <file> --token-nll          → per-token output
  python scripts/m2_visualize.py <run.json> --out=report.html
  python scripts/m2_compare.py --notations=csl,apl,prose
  python scripts/m2_quality.py eval/paraphrases/
  python scripts/m2_audit.py --verify
  bash scripts/m2_install_models.sh

§§ CI-INTEGRATION
  default : skip T25-gates ← models too-large for-fast-CI
  nightly : full T25 with-cache
  release-prep : T25 must-pass before-tag
  fast-suite : test_m2_harness.py with-mock-model only
  full-suite (nightly) : real-models + all-stratification

