§ THEORETICAL-NOTES ← §§ T25-depth-hints
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Perplexity foundations :
    PPL = exp(-Σᵢ log P(xᵢ|x<ᵢ) / N)
    NLL-per-token = -log P(token|context) / 1
    bits-per-token = NLL / ln(2)
    cross-entropy ≡ NLL ← language-model context
  Why m₂ ¬ raw-perplexity :
    raw-PPL : single-model bias dominates
    raw-PPL : doesn't normalize for-content-difficulty
    m₂ = ratio cancels content-difficulty per-paraphrase-pair
    m₂ : LLM serves as-density-detector ¬ judge-of-quality
  Multi-model rationale :
    single-model : confound model-familiarity with-density
    multi-model : agreement-pattern reveals model-independent signal
    Llama + Qwen + Mistral = different pre-training corpora
  Bootstrap CI :
    parametric assumes-Gaussian (often-violated in-NLL)
    non-parametric (bootstrap) more-robust
    1000 resamples = standard-default
    percentile-method simplest + valid for-large-n
  Paraphrase-quality :
    embedding-cosine : semantic-similarity proxy
    BLEU : surface-overlap (poor-fit for-paraphrases)
    BERTScore : contextual-embeddings (good-fit but-heavy)
    recommend : sentence-transformers cosine + entity-recall
  Comparison-harness pitfalls :
    APL/Lojban : LLMs unfamiliar ← high-NLL ← unfair-comparison
    interpretation-note : NLL measures familiarity ¬ density-alone
    document this caveat prominently
  Reproducibility :
    GGUF-checkpoint SHA-256 pin
    llama.cpp version-pin
    seed-fix + temp=0 + top-k=1
    deterministic across-runs ← R16 anchor
  Audit-chain reuse :
    smt_audit Ed25519 infrastructure already-shipped
    just-call from-Python via-subprocess parser.exe
    OR re-implement Python-Ed25519 (cryptography lib)
    recommend Python-native ∵ harness is-Python anyway

